roqsim_sensors/models/oakd/oakd.xml ships NO vendor geometry: the device is a box at the source
URDF's own collision dimensions, the same stand-in roqsim_mobile's turtlebot4 uses. Nothing here is
redistributed artwork.

What IS derived from a third party is every number in that file -- the box size and offset, the
camera's position and orientation, its 56.84 deg fovy (the Gazebo `horizontal_fov` of 1.25 rad
re-expressed vertically at 320x240), and the 0.075 m stereo baseline. They come from:

    https://github.com/ros-navigation/nav2_minimal_turtlebot_simulation
    (nav2_minimal_tb4_description/urdf/sensors/oakd.urdf.xacro)

